## 5. Fresh repository-state authentication

Before staging anything, independently authenticate current repository state.

Report at minimum:

- repository root;
- branch;
- upstream;
- local HEAD;
- tracking HEAD;
- fresh live remote research-branch HEAD;
- ahead/behind;
- parent/tree;
- index identity;
- staged state;
- tracked modifications;
- untracked files;
- material ignored files;
- substantive refs;
- `git diff --check`.

Previously reviewed baseline HEAD:

`063d823dc97f1a3690e26f8bb328385acb9d0aef`

Do not assume it is still current.

If any substantive drift invalidates the reviewed integration package:
- STOP;
- preserve exact drift;
- do not silently rebase the package.

Operational ignored mutation alone is not automatically blocking; apply claim-specific materiality.

## 6. Freeze exact publication scope

Before staging:

- enumerate exactly the 37 reviewed additions;
- verify no extra path is included;
- verify no reviewed path changed since integration review;
- record exact byte/LF/SHA-256 identities;
- recompute the canonical delta;
- require exact match to:
  `2e64bc07720a8e91b387724704d44860ee9a16fb5d5e364b46c11c5f97c12b1b`.

Do not modify any reviewed package member merely to make publication easier.

If any package byte differs:
- STOP;
- do not repair silently.

## 7. Stage exact reviewed package only

If and only if all checks pass:

- stage exactly the 37 reviewed additions;
- stage no unrelated file;
- verify index contains exactly the reviewed package delta;
- verify staged bytes match the reviewed identities;
- verify `git diff --cached --check`;
- verify no unstaged substantive mutation has become a dependency of the publication claim.

Freeze the exact staged-delta identity.

## 8. Commit authorization semantics

Create one commit containing exactly the reviewed 37 additions.

The commit message must make clear that it adopts/publishes the reviewed repository integration package but does NOT establish or activate N0.

Do not include language equivalent to:
- N0 established;
- N0 active;
- CD authorized;
- preflight passed;
- mining ready.

After commit, authenticate:

- commit SHA;
- sole parent;
- tree;
- exact file list;
- exact blobs;
- commit message;
- index state;
- working tree state.

The commit itself is only repository adoption/publication state unless the governing activation contract says otherwise.

## 9. Push exact commit

If commit authentication passes and no drift appears:

- push exactly the current research branch commit;
- do not alter persistent Git configuration;
- independently query the live remote after push;
- require live remote branch HEAD to equal the committed SHA;
- require ahead/behind 0/0.

If transport fails:
- bounded retry is permitted;
- do not weaken verification;
- do not change repository semantics to force success.

## 10. Publication receipt

Produce a frozen publication/adoption receipt recording at minimum:

- pre-publication baseline HEAD;
- reviewed canonical delta identity;
- integration PASS verdict identity;
- C6 PASS binding;
- commit SHA;
- parent;
- tree;
- exact published paths/blobs;
- post-push remote branch equality;
- index/working-tree state;
- durable-anchor availability;
- all preserved historical ceilings;
- upstream ORE obligation;
- exact authority ceiling:
  N0 is still NOT activated unless later activation prerequisites are separately satisfied.

The receipt must explicitly distinguish:

`repository adoption/publication complete`

from

`N0 activation complete`

These are not the same event.

## 11. Preserve historical ledger

Do not change any historical status.

Preserve:

- unavailable 3,288-byte listing;
- historical continuity U;
- historical non-consumption U;
- historical alias-exclusion U;
- historical direct-vs-symbolic U;
- historical symbolic-target U;
- producer/task/transaction history U;
- `IR-U1=U`;
- historical `CS23=U`;
- historical `CS-PREFLIGHT-U`;
- original N0 U/BLOCK;
- C2 incomplete;
- C3 FAIL/BLOCK;
- C4 FAIL/BLOCK;
- C5 FAIL/BLOCK;
- 179 historical D/U targets;
- 23 inherited D nodes;
- all other FAIL/U/withdrawn findings.

`RR-AR-PASS` remains architecture-only.

## 12. Preserve CD ceiling

Even after successful commit/push/publication, preserve:

`CD prospectively dependency-eligible`

only as a reviewed documentary dependency statement.

CD substantive work remains blocked until the effective N0 activation sequence and prospective preflight authorize it.

Do not execute:
`FOCUSED CD AUTHOR CORRECTION — LIVE CANARY`

in this lane.

## 13. Preserve upstream ORE requirement

Keep exactly:

`UPSTREAM ORE COMPATIBILITY / DRIFT CONTROL = REQUIRED and UNSATISFIED`

for eventual real-SOL readiness.

Do not mark compatibility satisfied.
Do not weaken drift/requalification/fail-closed requirements.

## 14. Activation boundary

After successful repository adoption/publication, determine the exact next required activation step from the reviewed activation contract.

Do NOT self-activate N0 merely because:

- the commit exists;
- push succeeded;
- remote equality is true;
- integration review passed.

If the activation contract requires independent publication verification before activation, preserve that requirement and route to it.

The expected sequence remains conceptually:

repository integration PASS
→ adoption/commit/publication
→ independent publication verification
→ N0 activation
→ prospective preflight
→ focused CD author correction

Do not collapse any step.

## 15. Final validation

Before completing:

- verify exact published commit/remote equality;
- verify no unrelated staged/committed file;
- verify reviewed package bytes unchanged;
- verify all durable anchors retrievable;
- verify continuation checkpoint/current-next-gate remain semantically correct after publication;
- verify they do not falsely claim N0 active;
- verify no CD substantive authority appears;
- verify historical U/FAIL ledger unchanged;
- verify upstream ORE remains REQUIRED and UNSATISFIED;
- verify no implementation or readiness authority is inferred.

Run relevant documentary tests with cache/bytecode writes disabled where practical.

## 16. Output and next gate

If staging, commit and publication all complete successfully:

Report and freeze:

- exact commit SHA;
- parent;
- tree;
- published paths/blobs;
- publication receipt identity;
- live remote branch equality;
- ahead/behind;
- working/index state;
- exact preserved ceilings;
- exact next gate.

N0 must still be reported as NOT ACTIVATED unless the separately required activation gate has been independently satisfied.

Authorize exactly one next gate:

`FRESH INDEPENDENT HIGH-RISK REVIEW — ORE N0 PUBLICATION / ACTIVATION READINESS`

That next gate must independently verify the published commit and determine whether the activation contract's prerequisites are satisfied and whether N0 activation may proceed.

Do not execute that review in this lane.

If publication cannot complete exactly:
- STOP;
- preserve exact blocker;
- do not manufacture activation authority.
